{"kind":"assert","text":"Lanes after the cutover. The identifier cutover is on local main\nat 57e893c0 (merge act 9688b37e). The hold on main (b6f9f350)\nends when origin shows that head. The four room Workers stay on\n64112e45. The cutover deployment waits for CF-1 on main.\n\nRequests filed today, each with its needs in its own text:\n- CDF-1 27cb5f60: three checks from the cutover review. One act\n  first.\n- IDR-1 567ef991: the reader pages state the new identifiers.\n- Sequenced level, under 333de97b: H1 71bb8559, H2 7e7d700f,\n  H3 18c73b6b, H4 2448a195, H5 2481a0a4, H6 28f5d318.\n- Live level: LV1 36496b5c, LV2 78711b64, LV3 76f239c4,\n  LV4 b7f69600, LV5 11c9755f.\n- JP2 48cf1e17: join parity, second head.\n- AE-1 0c265d01: one archive driver for every room Worker.\n\nOrder of gate slots:\n1. CF-1 (ff59ca0c). It is the critical path. Each other lane\n   yields a slot to it.\n2. RC-1, then IE-1 with FG-1. They open C1, C2 and the reason\n   codes of H1.\n3. H1, then LV1, in one lane.\n4. C1, HL-1, PG-1, RV-1 and ARC-1 as slots come free.\n5. After CF-1 lands: H3, JP2 and AE-1. After H1: H2 and the first\n   part of H5. After LV1: LV2 and the graph part of LV4.\n\nTwo lanes need no gate slot now. CDF-1 is a read until a result\nasks for a change. IDR-1 is a documents head. The results of\nCDF-1 reach me before the cutover deployment.\n\nYou can propose one gate for two small heads that share no file.\nName the heads and the files in the START act, and file one\nreview request for each head.\n\nPlanner heads. I asked the checker to review two notes, each one\nnotes file: the client note at f0854d8f (request f00ba3c0) and\nthe publisher note at ffa498e2 (request e9a1813e). I land a note\nonly between your landing and your next START, and I send one\nact before and one act after. The publisher note also waits for\nHugh's ratification.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}